COMMAND: ['/data2/build/egg-source-check-jomhn1so/target/release/solve', '--help']
Solve Rubik's cube scrambles from stdin optimally (fewest moves, any face turn is one move)

Usage: solve [OPTIONS] [TABLE] [SCRAMBLE]...

Arguments:
  [TABLE]
          The table file (made by `gen`, e.g. `gen 8 auto h8`) [with --fast: the largest found]

  [SCRAMBLE]...
          With --fast: the scramble (moves as arguments, or one quoted string) [default: a random 25-move scramble]

Options:
      --table <TABLE>
          The table file (as TABLE)
          
          [env: EGG_SOLVER_TABLE=]

  -t, --threads <THREADS>
          Threads
          
          [env: EGG_SOLVER_THREADS=]
          [default: 8]

  -l, --lanes <LANES>
          Interleaved lanes per thread [default: from `<TABLE>.tune` if `bench tune` made one, else a default for the table's size]

  -c, --concurrency <CONCURRENCY>
          Cubes in progress at once: 1 solves one cube at a time with all threads (lowest latency); 0 the whole input as a batch (highest throughput)
          
          [default: 0]

  -n, --count <COUNT>
          Solve only the first COUNT scrambles

      --json
          Print JSON lines: one object per cube, then the total (with --fast: one object)

      --fast
          Solve one scramble (the arguments, or a random 25-move one) as fast as this machine can and show the time: the largest table found (hK, K from 11 down, in /mnt/huge, /data2/tables, /data/tables, ./tables), all threads on the one cube (-c 1), after a warm-up cube; the time is the cube's own (table load excluded). Don't run it beside other heavy jobs: they share the cores and the time

      --warmup <SCRAMBLE>
          With --fast: the cube solved first, to warm up threads, caches and TLBs ("" for none) [default: a fixed 25-move scramble]

      --load <auto|map|copy|shm>
          How to load the table: `map` the file, `copy` it into memory (with transparent huge pages), `shm`: attach its shared memory segment, made from the file first if there is none (Linux; the segment stays until reboot or `solve --shm-remove`, see README.md "Shared memory"), or `auto`: the table's segment if one is there, else map on hugetlbfs, /dev/shm and other systems than Linux, else copy
          
          [env: EGG_SOLVER_LOAD=]
          [default: auto]

      --shm
          The same as `--load shm` (and overrides it)

      --prefault <0|1>
          With `map` and `shm`: read (map) the whole table at start (1), or each page on first use (0)
          
          [env: EGG_SOLVER_PREFAULT=]
          [default: 1]

      --shm-pages <LIST>
          With `shm`: the page sizes a new segment may get, tried largest first (1g and 2m pages come from the kernel's hugetlb pool)
          
          [env: EGG_SOLVER_SHM_PAGES=]
          [default: 1g,2m,4k]

      --shm-key <KEY>
          The shared memory segment's key [default: 0x636f (ASCII "co"), then the table's k and base, a byte each: 0x636f0709 for h7 base 9]
          
          [env: EGG_SOLVER_SHM_KEY=]

      --shm-load <TABLE>
          Load TABLE into its shared memory segment (as `--shm` does, if it is not there yet), print the segment and exit: later runs on TABLE attach it at once

      --shm-remove <TABLE>
          Remove TABLE's shared memory segment (as `ipcrm -M KEY`) and exit: its memory is freed once no process has it attached

  -v, --verbose...
          Log diagnostics to stderr (table loading and pages, threads, lanes); -vv for more. `RUST_LOG` (e.g. `debug`) overrides it

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Output, one line per cube in completion order, then a summary:
  solved <index> <length> <nodes> <seconds> <solution>
  total <cubes> cubes wall <s> wall/cube <s> nodes/cube <n> threads <t> lanes <l> concurrency <c>
<seconds> is the cube's time from its start to its solution (with -c 1, its
latency). Every solution is verified: a wrong one is reported as BAD <index>
and makes the exit status 1. With --json, the same as JSON lines:
  {"type":"solved","index":..,"moves":..,"length":..,"nodes":..,"lookups":..,"seconds":..,"ok":true}
  {"type":"total","cubes":..,"wall":..,"wall_per_cube":..,"nodes_per_cube":..,"threads":..,"lanes":..,"concurrency":..}

With --fast:
  table    <path>
  threads  <t> (all on this one cube)
  scramble <moves>
  solution <moves>
  length   <n> moves (optimal, verified)
  time     <ms> ms   (<n> M nodes, <rate> M nodes/s)
(with --json one object: table, threads, lanes, scramble, solution, length,
nodes, lookups, seconds, ms, nodes_per_second).

COMMAND: ['/data2/build/egg-source-check-jomhn1so/target/release/gen', '--help']
Generate, check and convert pruning tables (`hK` files)

Usage: gen [OPTIONS] <K> <BASE|auto> <OUT> [K:BASE:PATH]...
       gen <COMMAND>

Commands:
  generate  Generate hK into a file (the default command)
  stamp     Add a trailer to a table file made before trailers (in place: the trailer goes after the data, which is never written)
  check     Recompute a table's distribution and checksum and compare them with its trailer
  derive    hK of the source's base from a table of a larger k (min-collapse)
  compare   Compare table A with table B (of the same base; B's k at least A's, collapsed to A's k on the fly)
  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Arguments:
  <K>               The table: hK for K = 0..11 (larger: faster solves, more memory: h8 3.6 GiB, h11 58 GiB)
  <BASE|auto>       The base (0..12), or `auto` for the measured best for K
  <OUT>             The table file to write (data, then a trailer with K, base, distribution and checksum)
  [K:BASE:PATH]...  Smaller tables to derive in the same run (BFS only: K 0 or 11)

Options:
  -t, --threads <THREADS>  Threads [env: EGG_SOLVER_THREADS=] [default: 8]
      --parts <N>          Generate N row ranges one after the other (memory: 1/N of the table; time: up to N times; depth-first generation only) [default: 1]
      --dfs                Generate h0 by depth-first passes (as h1..h10), not by BFS: a check of one generator against the other
      --force              Skip the checks before the run: room for the files (free space, or free huge pages on hugetlbfs) and memory (`MemAvailable`)
  -v, --verbose...         Log diagnostics to stderr (table loading and pages, threads, lanes); -vv for more. `RUST_LOG` (e.g. `debug`) overrides it
  -h, --help               Print help
  -V, --version            Print version

